@@ ============================================================
@@ AtWt — the standard atomic weight of an element, as an interval
@@ Input : Z, symbol or name.  Output: Ar°, interval a…b (CIAAW 2024)
@@ The CIAAW gives either an interval [a, b] or a value v(U); both mean
@@ that the atomic weight of normal materials lies from a to b, or from
@@ v−U to v+U. Use AtWtσ for a value with a standard uncertainty.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================
  → x
  «
    x ⓁElmData 4 GET
    IF DUP "—" == THEN
      DROP "AtWt: no standard atomic weight" DoError
    END
  »
»
